\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The same comparison for the response to the archived \emph  {reference} spectrum, $a_m=r_m(B)$. Every fill is learned from that reference's own retained bins. Correlation is with the original reference response on the primary remote mass set. Poor polynomial interpolation can create additional structure; a smaller or larger ratio does not rank physical background models.\relax }}{133}{table.caption.114}\protected@file@percent }
